 "briefing": "# Infosys Briefing: 16 October to 15 November 2026\n\n## Research Status\n\nNo verified developments for Infosys in the 16 October to 15 November 2026 window could be confirmed. Every search returned no results, and no primary source page could be retrieved. This briefing therefore contains no reported news, launches, hires, or deals. The absence of results does not show that no qualifying events occurred. It means only that this research could not check them.\n\n## News\n\nNo qualifying news items were verified for the window. No dated summaries are available, and no claims are made about company announcements, results, guidance, or market-moving events. The official newsroom should be checked directly before the meeting ([1]).\n\n## Product and Service Launches\n\nNo product, platform, or service launches were verified for the window. Searches covering Infosys's AI, cloud, cybersecurity, and industry offerings returned no results. Launch announcements should be checked in the newsroom ([1]) and in the wire services for the same dates.\n\n## Executive and Key Hires\n\nNo executive appointments, resignations, board changes, or key hires were verified for the window. Leadership changes are typically disclosed to exchanges and the SEC, so the investor relations page ([2]) and SEC filings ([3]) are the most reliable places to confirm them.\n\n## Deals, Contracts, and Partnerships\n\nNo contract wins, acquisitions, investments, alliances, or partnerships were verified for the window. Material deals are usually disclosed through exchange filings or Form 6-K filings with the SEC. These should be reviewed before the meeting ([2], [3]).\n\n## Recommended Verification Before 17 November\n\n- **Newsroom:** Filter press releases to 16 October to 15 November 2026 ([1]).\n- **Investor relations:** Review stock exchange announcements, results materials, and any shareholder notices ([2]).\n- **SEC filings:** Check Infosys's Form 6-K filings for the window ([3]).\n- **Exchange filings:** Review NSE and BSE corporate announcements for the same dates. These sites were not accessed in this research.\n- **Business press:** Confirm dates and details against Economic Times, Mint, Business Standard, Moneycontrol, Reuters, and Bloomberg, which were not accessed in this research.\n\n## Open Questions for the Meeting\n\n1. Which news, product or service launches, leadership changes, and deals did Infosys disclose between 16 October and 15 November 2026, and can you confirm the announcement dates and the filings that support them?\n2. Have there been any changes to the CEO, CFO, or board, or any senior hires or departures announced or planned, that could affect strategy or governance in the coming months?\n3. Which contract wins, acquisitions, investments, or partnerships were announced or closed in the window, and are any still subject to regulatory approval or pending final terms?\n\n### Sources\n\n[1] Infosys Newsroom, Press Releases (not retrieved; for verification): https://www.infosys.com/newsroom/press-releases.html\n[2] Infosys Investor Relations (not retrieved; for verification): https://investors.infosys.com\n[3] SEC EDGAR Browse, Infosys Ltd filings (not retrieved; for verification): https://www.sec.gov/cgi-bin/browse-edgar",
